WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.370
Much like Shanks or Blackbeard before him,
Kizaru is an elaborate, carefully constructed

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:11.680
puzzle box of a character that no matter how
closely you look at, always seems to be missing

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.150
some essential pieces to reveal its full picture.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.200
This shouldn´t come as a big surprise, since
he only has received very limited screen time

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.870
in the story so far.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.380
Thoughtfully planed character development
after all, is one of the most crucial parts

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.480
in creating a vivid and capturing story line.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:35.070
And as we know, what is most needed for genuine
and organic character development, is especially

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.180
one thing: Time.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:42.649
So, one would think that having only limited
screen time for such an enormous cast as One

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:48.040
Piece, would be a striking disadvantage, resulting
in shallow characters with little room for

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.829
emotional involvement.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:55.570
And yet, it´s EXACTLY characters like Kizaru,
Shanks or Blackbeard that have readers most

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.570
excited.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.610
So, what is the secret behind this apparent
paradox?

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:05.920
The answer to that is simple: Oda is a master
of mystery.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.459
He takes the apparent handicap of certain
characters in the story and turns it into

00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:11.459
a strength.

00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:16.100
He makes use of every single panel, that this
character is shown in, to fletch out a certain

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.899
image for his audience.

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:22.999
However, compared to characters with more
screen time, he doesn´t give them slow, organic

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:24.579
growth over time.

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:29.179
Much rather he hands us little puzzle pieces
of information about that person.

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:33.670
Based on these pieces you can create a rough
image of the character in your mind.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:39.229
However, these pieces can be turned and rearranged
in different ways, and thus allow for different

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:41.359
interpretations and perspectives.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:46.770
A great example for this are all the small
pieces we have gathered for Blackbeard.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.450
Many of them are so different that you can
puzzle together various possible images for

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.719
his character.

00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:55.649
In some scenes he seems to be goofy.

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.450
In others he seems cruel.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.450
And in again others he seems straight out
scared.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.969
This impression of inconsistency is complemented
by his mysterious power to consume multiple

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:10.580
devil fruits as well his ambition to become
pirate king.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.500
It is really barely more than a handful of
clues about who Blackbeard is.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.830
And yet, he might be the most heatedly discussed
character in the entire series.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:27.720
The same applies to Shanks about whom we also
only hold tiny bits and pieces.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.390
And of course, one of the characters that
can´t be left out of this list, is Kizaru.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:38.060
Being the Admiral, that we know by far the
least about, with the exception of Ryokugyo

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:44.110
of course, Kizaru is a prime example of how
Oda manages to create amazing characters,

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:49.970
by only giving them a basic set of traits
and leaving the rest ambiguous and unclear.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:55.000
How fitting then, that Kizaru follows the
path of unclear justice.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.200
And even though, there only is so much that
we know about his personality and role in

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.900
the story, Oda has left us enough pieces of
the puzzle to allow us to figure out what

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.900
it means.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.910
So, in this video, we will try to put together
the purpose Kizaru has in the story of One

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.910
Piece.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:17.620
And to do so, we will answer the most crucial
question surrounding his character: What is

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:24.000
unclear Justice ? Before we can look at his
ideological concept of morality and justice

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:31.430
however, we first have to understand, who
Kizaru is as a person.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:37.350
Same as with his fellow admirals, Borsalino
Kizaru is based on a famous Japanese actor.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:43.490
Thus, his conceptual design is heavily based
on a character played by actor Kunie Tanaka

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.960
in his youth.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.530
Beside their strikingly similar lineaments,
their similarities include Kizaru´s outfit,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.510
his birthday and even his real name, Borsalino.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:59.650
The epithet ‘Kizaru’, he acquired when
rising into the ranks of the admirals.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:04.750
Same as with his colleagues, this epithet
consists of a color and an animal.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:11.900
In Kizaru´s case this is Ki for Yellow and
Zaru for monkey, making him the yellow Monkey.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.910
Accordingly, Sakazuki is Aka-Inu, the red
dog.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:19.470
While Kuzan is Ao-Kiji, the blue pheasant.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:25.039
Oda chose these animals based on the famous
folktale of Momotaro, who befriended a pheasant,

00:04:25.039 --> 00:04:29.400
a dog and a monkey to accompany him on his
journey.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:35.110
Next to his very interesting visual and contextual
design, Kizaru is without a doubt also one

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.699
of the most powerful characters in the world
of One Piece.

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:43.870
In fact, based on his devil fruit, it is actually
quite hard to determine HOW strong he might

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.300
actually be.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.819
After all, being light itself, would easily
make him the fastest character in the story.

00:04:50.819 --> 00:04:55.860
Additionally, if Oda were to be more or less
physically accurate with his fruit, it would

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.669
most likely also make him the most overpowered
character.

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:04.069
However, we can assume that there are certain
limitations to that power.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:09.379
Nonetheless, we have never seen Kizaru go
all out before, so we don´t know what he

00:05:09.379 --> 00:05:11.680
might truly be capable of.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.389
Accordingly, we also do not know a lot about
Borsellino’s past.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:20.979
There is a single image of him as a child,
suggesting him to be rather kind and smart,

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:23.189
while brooding over a pile of books.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:29.090
We know that he joined the marines at a young
age, around the same time as Sakazuki.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:34.059
Similar to his peer, he quickly rose through
the ranks and reached the status of a vice-admiral

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:36.460
at a fairly young age.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:41.840
The only thing we know about his time then,
is that he was responsible for capturing Arlong

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.090
after Fisher Tiger´s death.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:49.189
Small fun fact regarding this panel: The hat
that Kizaru is wearing here is actually called

00:05:49.189 --> 00:05:54.540
a Borsalino, which is the name of Italy´s
oldest manufacturer of luxury hats.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.540
See.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.360
We are learning stuff about the world, while
taking about One Piece.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.039
Isn´t that fun?

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:01.120
Moving on.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:07.289
The most defining arc for Kizaru´s character
is undoubtably Sabaody, where he is sent after

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:10.479
Luffy´s attack on one of the Tenryubito.

00:06:10.479 --> 00:06:15.719
While he has no problem taking on the entirety
of the worst generation on his own, he doesn´t

00:06:15.719 --> 00:06:19.779
manage to catch even a single one of them
in the end, being hindered by Rayleigh´s

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.029
and Kuma´s interception in his pursuit.

00:06:22.029 --> 00:06:26.960
While he is one of the strongest forces present
during the war at Marineford and taking on

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.789
the likes of Whitebeard and Marco singlehandedly,
he doesn´t play any major role in the war´s

00:06:32.789 --> 00:06:33.789
outcome.

00:06:33.789 --> 00:06:38.879
What really stands out about Kizaru´s character,
therefore, are not his actions, but much rather

00:06:38.879 --> 00:06:40.719
his personality.

00:06:40.719 --> 00:06:44.909
And I´m not gonna lie, it´s one of my favorites
in the story so far.

00:06:44.909 --> 00:06:49.279
Oda depicts Kizaru as an easy-going and laid-back
person.

00:06:49.279 --> 00:06:54.939
In fact, he is so laid-back, that at times
he appears to be slow in his reactions and

00:06:54.939 --> 00:07:00.449
almost slothful, which has resulted in a number
of stoner jokes surrounding his character.

00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:04.219
And you guys better put some good ones in
the comments.

00:07:04.219 --> 00:07:08.509
What makes Kizaru a true favorite of mine
however, is the fact that he is one of the

00:07:08.509 --> 00:07:13.449
rare characters in the story that has a genuinely
sarcastic nature.

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:19.139
He often talks about how scary or shocking
a situation is, but completely lacks the corresponding

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:20.440
facial expression.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:26.669
In my personal opinion, characters with a
sarcastic take on things are immensely entertaining.

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:31.529
However, they are quite hard to write and
convey to a general audience, which is why

00:07:31.529 --> 00:07:34.979
they are so rarely found inside the Shounen
genre.

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:40.139
As a result, this trait gives Kizaru an air
of cleverness and sharpness, in comparison

00:07:40.139 --> 00:07:43.999
to other characters that take everything at
face value.

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:47.370
This impression is complemented by his cool
composure.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.840
No matter how intense a situation might be,
he always appears to be in control of his

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.960
emotions.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.839
To the reader, this conveys a sense of strong
confidence in his own abilities.

00:07:57.839 --> 00:08:03.309
We can see this in his absentmindedness during
battle, not fearing any damage, as well in

00:08:03.309 --> 00:08:06.840
his lack of awareness for collateral damage.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.979
Despite his immense battle strength, but maybe
in connection to his laid-back personality,

00:08:11.979 --> 00:08:15.469
Kizaru seems to lack personal ambition.

00:08:15.469 --> 00:08:19.999
Not only is he the only of the former three
admirals, that doesn´t aspire to become fleet

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:24.830
admiral, he also seems to have no interest
in authority in general.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:28.389
He doesn´t like giving orders but prefers
receiving them.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:33.320
We can even see him taking directions from
Sentomaru, one of his own subordinates.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.610
Nonetheless, Kizaru is deeply respected within
the ranks of the marines.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:43.240
His most defining trait, however, might be
his fearlessness.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:48.510
Not only does Borsalino take on Whitebeard
and the entire worst generation by himself,

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:53.750
but he even offers to go to Wano and confront
Kaido AND Big Mom on his own.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.550
Something that even Akainu is reluctant to
do.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:01.700
Now, as mentioned before, all these puzzle
pieces give us a rough image of Kizaru’s

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.700
character.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.630
However, we still lack the full image.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:10.690
For instance, we have no idea what Kizaru
actually values or what his great desire and

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.940
drive is.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:12.940
We have no idea why he joined the marines
in the first place or what his vision for

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:13.940
the world is.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.940
We can´t see it yet.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.090
It´s all.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.090
Unclear.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:22.240
What we DO know however, is that Kizaru shares
neither Akainu´s sense of absolute justice

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:27.240
and hate towards pirates nor Kuzan´s kind
and forgiving nature.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:33.010
He much rather appears like an old teacher,
that intervenes and lectures when necessary,

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:36.020
but stays out of everyone’s business otherwise.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:41.770
We even see him specifically targeting Luffy
to lecture him about the gap between him and

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.460
those on the battlefield.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:49.010
So, based on these insights we have gathered
now, let´s deconstruct what the concept of

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:57.030
unclear justice actually means and what it
tells us about Kizaru´s role in the story.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:01.500
Based on his personality and the construction
of his character, I would argue that there

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:07.030
are three distinct interpretations of Kizaru´s
concept of unclear justice.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:12.241
The first one of these is rather straight
forward: Kizaru´s justice is unclear, because

00:10:12.241 --> 00:10:17.770
he often seems indecisive and without directions
in his decisions and objectives.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:22.910
Back on Sabaody for instance, he immediately
delays his mission to look for Sentomaru.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:27.710
Once Sentomaru contacts him, he goes back
to looking for Luffy, before once again getting

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.240
sidetracked by the other supernova.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.410
Once he defeats them however, he doesn´t
bother to capture them, but once again leaves

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:39.750
to find the straw hats, finally ending up
not capturing any of them, but sacking 500

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.560
other pirates instead.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:46.190
It is quite possible, that this stems from
his sense of invincibility.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:51.270
Which makes you wonder, how powerful Kizaru
truly is, if he´s able to be this unfocused

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:52.830
in his actions.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:59.180
His way of decision making lacks a clear direction
and strive as Akainu and Aokiji do, which

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.490
makes it unclear.

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:05.910
And speaking of his two fellow admirals, this
brings us to the second way of looking at

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.470
his justice.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:12.100
Because it is especially unclear, when put
between the two extremes that are Akainu and

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.100
Aokiji.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:18.280
Kuzan´s justice is unclear, because it falls
on neither side of the spectrum.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:23.190
He neither follow´s Sakazuki´s absolute
justice, that is built on hatred towards all

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:29.810
pirates and militaristic strictness, nor Kuzan´s
lazy justice, that is based on morality and

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:30.810
fairness.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:36.380
Instead, as the Sabaody example shows really
well, Borsellino’s sense of justice seems

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.940
to be movable on the scale between red and
blue.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:44.670
Trying to capture the straw hats, failing,
but then capturing 500 other pirates in the

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:51.240
process shows us how his sense of just action
sways between thoroughness and fairness.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:55.640
While it might be very easy to agree with
one of the extreme positions, Kizaru might

00:11:55.640 --> 00:12:00.060
actually be the admiral that is the most objective
out of the three.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:05.860
Being neither unnecessarily cruel nor unnecessarily
forgiving, Kizaru can be seen as the balanced

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.330
middle between Akainu and Kuzan.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:13.700
Now, obviously this doesn´t take into account
how flawed and unjust the political structure

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:19.720
of the One Piece world is, which might arguably
make Kuzan´s path more justified, at least

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.510
for me personally.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:26.590
But based on the assumption that the marines
are a neutral organization in the service

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:31.950
of the people, Kizaru would bring the necessary
flexibility and flexibility in his actions.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:36.980
The thing is, that we don´t know what ideals
Kizaru follows and what his dream for the

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.220
world is.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:43.430
Which already brings us to the last meaning
of unclear justice: Oda deliberately keeps

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.050
Kizaru´s true nature unclear for us to see.

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:52.680
We still miss a few decisive pieces of the
puzzle to truly understand, who Kizaru is

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:53.680
as a person.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:58.910
So, I am fairly confident, that Kizaru will
have to play a major role in the future of

00:12:58.910 --> 00:12:59.970
the story.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:05.350
And once, we will learn more about him, we
might also get a better picture of him.

